          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Menachem Begin</strong><br>\nMenachem Begin was born in Brest-Litovsk, then part of the Russian Empire, on August 16, 1913. He grew up in a Jewish family that valued education and tradition. Begin attended the University of Warsaw, where he studied law and became active in Zionist movements, advocating for the Jewish homeland in Palestine.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Begin's Zionist Activities</strong><br>\nDuring the 1930s, Begin became a leader in the Zionist group Betar, which emphasized Jewish self-defense and the establishment of a Jewish state. He moved to Palestine in 1942, joining the Irgun, a militant organization opposed to British control.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Irgun and British Mandate Palestine</strong><br>\nAs the leader of Irgun from 1944 to 1948, Begin directed operations against the British authorities in Palestine. His aim was to force the British out and establish a Jewish state. The Irgun's activities were controversial and included attacks on British targets and participation in the Arab-Jewish conflict.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
