            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Lebanon War and Later Years</strong><br>\nDuring Begin's leadership, Israel faced the challenge of the Lebanon War in 1982, aiming to stop PLO attacks. The war's controversies and the death of his wife affected Begin deeply, leading to his resignation in 1983.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Retirement</strong><br>\nBegin spent the remainder of his life out of the public eye, passing away on March 9, 1992. He left a complex legacy as a Nobel Peace Prize laureate, a freedom fighter, and a leader who shaped Israel's destiny.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Remembering Begin</strong><br>\nMenachem Begin is remembered for his fiery oratory, his commitment to his people, and his role in establishing Israel as a sovereign nation. His life's journey from revolutionary to statesman is a significant chapter in Israeli history.</p>\n"
              },
